# In pull mode qtdemux sends the stream whose next sample decodes earliest, so
# its output is interleaved by time whatever the storage order. In push mode it
# sends samples in the order their bytes arrive, and a fragment may store each
# stream's samples as one run: legacy hlsdemux delivers fMP4 HLS segments with
# all of a segment's video before its audio. decodebin's buffering multiqueue
# then stops the demuxer 5 s into the run and the other stream's sink starves
# until playback drains it.
#
# With an upstream delivering timed fragments and more than one non-sparse
# stream, push-mode fragmented qtdemux holds the samples it takes and sends them
# in decode-time order. A held sample goes out once no other non-sparse stream
# can still provide an earlier one in the fragment it was taken from: that
# stream's next parsed sample, or the end of the samples parsed for it, is not
# before the held sample. The next timed fragment upstream delivers completes
# the previous one. Everything held is sent at upstream EOS, before a new TIME
# segment, at stream-start, at a real discont and before a second moov, and is
# dropped on reset.
#
# Applied by build_deps with patch -p1, after
# gst-plugins-good-qtdemux-upstream-stream-tags.patch.

